text of the license.

vkminer reuses the pool-protocol client and option handling of cpuminer-opt,
which descends from cpuminer (pooler) and cpuminer (Jeff Garzik). That code is
offered under "version 2 of the License, or (at your option) any later
version", and vkminer takes the later-version option. Files carried over from
cpuminer-opt keep their original copyright notices and their GPLv2-or-later
headers; the combined work is distributed under GPLv3. See AUTHORS.


Third-party components

Components vendored under third_party/ keep their own licenses, each in its
own subdirectory:

  volk                        MIT
  VulkanMemoryAllocator       MIT
  Vulkan-Headers              Apache-2.0 OR MIT

All are compatible with GPLv3. Note that Apache-2.0 is compatible with GPLv3
but not with GPLv2 -- one of the reasons this project is on version 3.
